# GEM line-ending policy.
#
# Git must never normalize line endings in this repository. The project's
# formatting discipline is enforced by gem_audit.py's `formatting` check, which
# fires RED with no autofix on any lone-LF in a .ttl file:
#
#   .ttl files  -> CRLF (except cpt.ttl, which is LF-authored)
#   .md / .json -> LF
#
# On Windows, git's default core.autocrlf=true would rewrite endings on checkout
# and corrupt GEM_policy_instances.ttl on the first clone. `* -text` disables
# all text detection and conversion, so the bytes committed are the bytes
# checked out.
#
# Do not replace this with per-extension eol= rules. Blanket -text is the whole
# point: it cannot be wrong about a file type it has not been told about.

* -text
